# Product-first execution

Before changing product behavior, identify:

- target user
- user problem
- desired outcome
- acceptance criteria
- non-goals
- dependencies and constraints

If these are already defined in repository documents, reuse them instead of rewriting them.

Do not invent metrics, customer claims, ROI, pricing, legal statements, integrations, or feature readiness.

When the user asks for an idea to be built but the implementation target is not yet precise, use the product-brief skill first.
